People 
Steve Menke, director of trading and marketing at Innovative Gas Services (IGS), has 
been named vice president and general manager of the company. He has been involved in 
energy marketing activities for more than 15 years. IGS, located in Owensboro, Ky., is a 
subsidiary of WBI Holdings, a unit of MDU Resources Group. 
Kansas City Power & Light has named Andrea Bielsker chief financial officer. She 
joined the company in 1984 as a financial planner and was appointed vice president and 
treasurer earlier this year. 
Bonneville Power Administrator Judi Johansen will become executive vice president 
for government affairs and regulation at PacifiCorp. Steve Wright, currently Bonneville 
Power’s deputy administrator, will become acting administrator when Johansen leaves. 
Exelon has named Randall Mehrberg senior vice president and general counsel. He 
was an equity partner with Jenner & Block. 
Duke Energy has elected Kirk Michael vice president and chief financial officer, finance 
and planning. Most recently, he was vice president of planning and finance for energy services, 
a department consisting of Duke Energy North America, Duke Energy International, 
Duke Energy Merchants, Duke Engineering & Services, Duke/Fluor Daniel and DukeSolutions. 
Stephen Gregorlo has joined Excelergy as vice president, chief financial officer and 
treasurer. He comes to the company from Vality Technology where he served as executive 
vice president and chief financial officer. 
Aquila Energy has selected Joe Stessman, Winston Balletyne and Gary Payne to its 
coal marketing and trading organization.                                    
